{"id":"mahabharata-9-011","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":11,"title":"एकादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 11 · Shalya's mace against Yudhishthira","summary":{"en":"On seeing his charioteer fall, Shalya takes up an iron club and fights Bhima in a fierce duel of maces. Yudhishthira is then struck by Shalya's arrows and is greatly distressed.","kn":"ಸಾರಥಿ ಬಿದ್ದುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡ ಶಲ್ಯ ಕಬ್ಬಿಣದ ಗದೆ ಹಿಡಿದು ಭೀಮನೊಡನೆ ಉಗ್ರ ಗದಾಯುದ್ಧ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಂತರ ಶಲ್ಯನ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಗಾಯಗೊಂಡು ತುಂಬ ಸಂಕಟಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सारथी को गिरता देख शल्य लोहे की गदा लेकर भीम से भीषण गदायुद्ध करता है। फिर शल्य के बाणों से युधिष्ठिर पीड़ित होकर बहुत व्यथित होते हैं।","te":"సారథి పడటం చూసి శల్యుడు ఇనుప గద తీసుకుని భీమునితో భీకర గదాయుద్ధం చేస్తాడు. తరువాత శల్యుని బాణాలతో యుధిష్ఠిరుడు గాయపడి చాలా బాధపడతాడు.","ta":"தேரோட்டி வீழ்வதைக் கண்ட சல்யன் இரும்புக் கதையை எடுத்துப் பீமனுடன் கடும் கதைப்போர் புரிகிறான். பின் சல்யனின் அம்புகளால் யுதிஷ்டிரர் காயமுற்றுப் பெரிதும் வருந்துகிறார்.","ml":"തന്റെ സാരഥി വീഴുന്നത് കണ്ട ശല്യൻ ഇരുമ്പുഗദയെടുത്ത് ഭീമനുമായി കടുത്ത ഗദായുദ്ധം നടത്തുന്നു. തുടർന്ന് ശല്യന്റെ അമ്പുകളേറ്റ് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ വലിയ ദുഃഖത്തിലാകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.11; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पतितं प्रेक्ष्य यन्तारं शल्यः सर्वायसीं गदाम् ।\nआदाय तरसा राजंस्तस्थौ गिरिरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his charioteer fallen, Shalya swiftly took up an all-iron mace, O king, and stood as unmoving as a mountain."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं दीप्तमिव कालाग्निं पाशहस्तमिवान्तकम् ।\nसशृङ्गमिव कैलासं सवज्रमिव वासवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, taking up his great mace, rushed at him swiftly, as Shalya stood like blazing fire at the world's end, like Death with a noose in hand, like Kailasa with its peaks, like Indra with his thunderbolt,"}},{"n":3,"text":"सशूलमिव हर्यक्षं वने मत्तमिव द्विपम् ।\nजवेनाभ्यपतद्भीमः प्रगृह्य महतीं गदाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"like a lion with a trident, like a rutting elephant in a forest."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः शङ्खप्रणादश्च तूर्याणां च सहस्रशः ।\nसिंहनादश्च संजज्ञे शूराणां हर्षवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then conches and thousands of trumpets sounded, and a lion's roar rose that cheered the brave."}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रेक्षन्तः सर्वतस्तौ हि योधा योधमहाद्विपौ ।\nतावकाश्च परे चैव साधु साध्वित्यथाब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the warriors, your men and the enemy, watching those two great elephants among fighters on every side, cried out, \"Well done, well done!\""}},{"n":6,"text":"न हि मद्राधिपादन्यो रामाद्वा यदुनन्दनात् ।\nसोढुमुत्सहते वेगं भीमसेनस्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"For none other than the lord of Madra, or Rama, or the delight of the Yadus, can bear Bhimasena's rush in battle."}},{"n":7,"text":"तथा मद्राधिपस्यापि गदावेगं महात्मनः ।\nसोढुमुत्सहते नान्यो योधो युधि वृकोदरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And in the same way, no other fighter in the fray than Bhima, the wolf-bellied, could bear the mace-rush of the great-souled lord of Madra."}},{"n":8,"text":"तौ वृषाविव नर्दन्तौ मण्डलानि विचेरतुः ।\nआवल्गितौ गदाहस्तौ मद्रराजवृकोदरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bellowing like two bulls, the king of Madras and Bhima circled in rings, mace in hand, leaping about."}},{"n":9,"text":"मण्डलावर्तमार्गेषु गदाविहरणेषु च ।\nनिर्विशेषमभूद्युद्धं तयोः पुरुषसिंहयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In circling, turning and wielding their maces, the fight between those two lions among men was entirely even."}},{"n":10,"text":"तप्तहेममयैः शुभ्रैर्बभूव भयवर्धनी ।\nअग्निज्वालैरिवाविद्धा पट्टैः शल्यस्य सा गदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya's mace, banded with bright strips of hot gold, flashed terrifyingly as it swung, like flames of fire."}},{"n":11,"text":"तथैव चरतो मार्गान्मण्डलेषु महात्मनः ।\nविद्युदभ्रप्रतीकाशा भीमस्य शुशुभे गदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way Bhima's mace, as that great-souled man moved in his circles, gleamed like lightning in a cloud."}},{"n":12,"text":"ताडिता मद्रराजेन भीमस्य गदया गदा ।\nदीप्यमानेव वै राजन्ससृजे पावकार्चिषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Shalya's mace struck Bhima's mace, O king, it seemed to blaze and threw out sparks of fire."}},{"n":13,"text":"तथा भीमेन शल्यस्य ताडिता गदया गदा ।\nअङ्गारवर्षं मुमुचे तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And when Bhima's mace struck Shalya's, it let loose a shower of embers, which was like a wonder."}},{"n":14,"text":"दन्तैरिव महानागौ शृङ्गैरिव महर्षभौ ।\nतोत्त्रैरिव तदान्योन्यं गदाग्राभ्यां निजघ्नतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They struck one another with the tips of their maces, as two great elephants strike with tusks, two great bulls with horns, or as men with goads."}},{"n":15,"text":"तौ गदानिहतैर्गात्रैः क्षणेन रुधिरोक्षितौ ।\nप्रेक्षणीयतरावास्तां पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their bodies beaten by maces and drenched in blood in a moment, they became more striking to see, like two flowering kimshuka trees."}},{"n":16,"text":"गदया मद्रराजेन सव्यदक्षिणमाहतः ।\nभीमसेनो महाबाहुर्न चचालाचलो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck on left and right by the mace of the king of Madras, mighty-armed Bhimasena did not budge, like a mountain."}},{"n":17,"text":"तथा भीमगदावेगैस्ताड्यमानो मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nशल्यो न विव्यथे राजन्दन्तिनेवाहतो गिरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Shalya, struck again and again by the rushes of Bhima's mace, was not shaken, O king, like a mountain hit by an elephant."}},{"n":18,"text":"शुश्रुवे दिक्षु सर्वासु तयोः पुरुषसिंहयोः ।\nगदानिपातसंह्रादो वज्रयोरिव निस्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In all directions was heard the crash of the falling maces of those two lions among men, like the sound of two thunderbolts."}},{"n":19,"text":"निवृत्य तु महावीर्यौ समुच्छ्रितगदावुभौ ।\nपुनरन्तरमार्गस्थौ मण्डलानि विचेरतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two mighty heroes, drawing back with maces raised, again stood in the ring and moved in their circles in the space between."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथाभ्येत्य पदान्यष्टौ संनिपातोऽभवत्तयोः ।\nउद्यम्य लोहदण्डाभ्यामतिमानुषकर्मणोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then after stepping up eight paces they clashed, raising their iron clubs, in deeds beyond human power."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रार्थयानौ तदान्योऽन्यं मण्डलानि विचेरतुः ।\nक्रियाविशेषं कृतिनौ दर्शयामासतुस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each seeking the other, they went round in rings, and those skilled men showed special feats of skill."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथोद्यम्य गदे घोरे सशृङ्गाविव पर्वतौ ।\nतावाजघ्नतुरन्योन्यं यथा भूमिचलेऽचलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, raising the dreadful maces, they struck each other like two horned mountains in an earthquake."}},{"n":23,"text":"तौ परस्परवेगाच्च गदाभ्यां च भृशाहतौ ।\nयुगपत्पेततुर्वीरावुभाविन्द्रध्वजाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hit hard by each other's force and by the maces, both heroes fell at the same moment, like two banners of Indra."}},{"n":24,"text":"उभयोः सेनयोर्वीरास्तदा हाहाकृतोऽभवन् ।\nभृशं मर्मण्यभिहतावुभावास्तां सुविह्वलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a cry of dismay went up from the heroes of both armies; both lay badly struck in vital parts, greatly dazed."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः सगदमारोप्य मद्राणामृषभं रथे ।\nअपोवाह कृपः शल्यं तूर्णमायोधनादपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kripa lifted Shalya, bull of the Madras, with his mace onto his chariot and swiftly carried him away from the battlefield."}},{"n":26,"text":"क्षीबवद्विह्वलत्वात्तु निमेषात्पुनरुत्थितः ।\nभीमसेनो गदापाणिः समाह्वयत मद्रपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, who had been stunned as if drunk, rose again in a moment and, mace in hand, challenged the lord of Madra."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततस्तु तावकाः शूरा नानाशस्त्रसमायुताः ।\nनानावादित्रशब्देन पाण्डुसेनामयोधयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your brave warriors, bearing weapons of every kind and amid the noise of many instruments, fought the Pandava army."}},{"n":28,"text":"भुजावुच्छ्रित्य शस्त्रं च शब्देन महता ततः ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्महाराज दुर्योधनपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, with arms and weapons raised and with a great shout, they charged, with Duryodhana at their head."}},{"n":29,"text":"तदनीकमभिप्रेक्ष्य ततस्ते पाण्डुनन्दनाः ।\nप्रययुः सिंहनादेन दुर्योधनवधेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that force, the sons of Pandu advanced with lion roars, eager to kill Duryodhana."}},{"n":30,"text":"तेषामापततां तूर्णं पुत्रस्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nप्रासेन चेकितानं वै विव्याध हृदये भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they rushed swiftly on, best of Bharatas, your son struck Chekitana hard in the heart with a lance."}},{"n":31,"text":"स पपात रथोपस्थे तव पुत्रेण ताडितः ।\nरुधिरौघपरिक्लिन्नः प्रविश्य विपुलं तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by your son, he fell onto the seat of his chariot, drenched in streams of blood, entering deep darkness."}},{"n":32,"text":"चेकितानं हतं दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवानां महारथाः ।\nप्रसक्तमभ्यवर्षन्त शरवर्षाणि भागशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Chekitana slain, the great warriors of the Pandavas showered arrows in groups without pause."}},{"n":33,"text":"तावकानामनीकेषु पाण्डवा जितकाशिनः ।\nव्यचरन्त महाराज प्रेक्षणीयाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the divisions of your side, the victorious Pandavas moved about, a sight to see on every side, great king."}},{"n":34,"text":"कृपश्च कृतवर्मा च सौबलश्च महाबलः ।\nअयोधयन्धर्मराजं मद्रराजपुरस्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, Kritavarman and mighty Shakuni, son of Subala, with the king of Madras at their head, fought the king of dharma."}},{"n":35,"text":"भारद्वाजस्य हन्तारं भूरिवीर्यपराक्रमम् ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज धृष्टद्युम्नमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, great king, fought Dhrishtadyumna, the slayer of Bharadvaja's son, a man of great strength and prowess."}},{"n":36,"text":"त्रिसाहस्रा रथा राजंस्तव पुत्रेण चोदिताः ।\nअयोधयन्त विजयं द्रोणपुत्रपुरस्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three thousand chariots, sent by your son, with Drona's son at their head, fought for victory."}},{"n":37,"text":"विजये धृतसंकल्पाः समभित्यक्तजीविताः ।\nप्राविशंस्तावका राजन्हंसा इव महत्सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Resolved on victory and having given up their lives, your men plunged in, O king, like swans into a great lake."}},{"n":38,"text":"ततो युद्धमभूद्घोरं परस्परवधैषिणाम् ।\nअन्योन्यवधसंयुक्तमन्योन्यप्रीतिवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a terrible fight began between men who wanted to kill one another, bound up in mutual killing and a growing fondness for each other."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्मिन्प्रवृत्ते संग्रामे राजन्वीरवरक्षये ।\nअनिलेनेरितं घोरमुत्तस्थौ पार्थिवं रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that battle went on, great king, with its heroes falling, a fierce cloud of dust rose, stirred by the wind."}},{"n":40,"text":"श्रवणान्नामधेयानां पाण्डवानां च कीर्तनात् ।\nपरस्परं विजानीमो ये चायुध्यन्नभीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By hearing the names and the Pandavas' shouted calls, we could tell who was who among those who fought fearlessly."}},{"n":41,"text":"तद्रजः पुरुषव्याघ्र शोणितेन प्रशामितम् ।\nदिशश्च विमला जज्ञुस्तस्मिन्रजसि शामिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"That dust, tiger among men, was settled by blood, and when it had settled the directions grew clear."}},{"n":42,"text":"तथा प्रवृत्ते संग्रामे घोररूपे भयानके ।\nतावकानां परेषां च नासीत्कश्चित्पराङ्मुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the battle, so frightening and terrible, went on in this way, none on your side or the enemy's turned his back."}},{"n":43,"text":"ब्रह्मलोकपरा भूत्वा प्रार्थयन्तो जयं युधि ।\nसुयुद्धेन पराक्रान्ता नराः स्वर्गमभीप्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Set on the world of Brahma, seeking victory in battle, those men, valiant in fair fight and desiring heaven,"}},{"n":44,"text":"भर्तृपिण्डविमोक्षार्थं भर्तृकार्यविनिश्चिताः ।\nस्वर्गसंसक्तमनसो योधा युयुधिरे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"bent on freeing themselves from the debt of their master's food and sure of their duty to him, fought then with their minds fixed on heaven."}},{"n":45,"text":"नानारूपाणि शस्त्राणि विसृजन्तो महारथाः ।\nअन्योन्यमभिगर्जन्तः प्रहरन्तः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great warriors, loosing weapons of many kinds, roaring at one another and striking one another,"}},{"n":46,"text":"हत विध्यत गृह्णीत प्रहरध्वं निकृन्तत ।\nइति स्म वाचः श्रूयन्ते तव तेषां च वै बले ॥","meaning":{"en":"in your army and theirs these cries were heard: \"Kill! Pierce! Seize! Strike! Cut down!\""}},{"n":47,"text":"ततः शल्यो महाराज धर्मराजं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nविव्याध निशितैर्बाणैर्हन्तुकामो महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shalya, great king, wishing to kill the great warrior King Yudhishthira, pierced him with sharp arrows."}},{"n":48,"text":"तस्य पार्थो महाराज नाराचान्वै चतुर्दश ।\nमर्माण्युद्दिश्य मर्मज्ञो निचखान हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava, knowing vital spots, smiling as it were, planted fourteen iron arrows in Shalya aimed at his vital parts, great king."}},{"n":49,"text":"तं वार्य पाण्डवं बाणैर्हन्तुकामो महायशाः ।\nविव्याध समरे क्रुद्धो बहुभिः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing to kill the Pandava, glorious Shalya parried him, and in rage pierced him with many heron-feathered arrows in the battle."}},{"n":50,"text":"अथ भूयो महाराज शरेण नतपर्वणा ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं समाजघ्ने सर्वसैन्यस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then once more, great king, Shalya struck Yudhishthira with an arrow with bent joints, in sight of the whole army."}},{"n":51,"text":"धर्मराजोऽपि संक्रुद्धो मद्रराजं महायशाः ।\nविव्याध निशितैर्बाणैः कङ्कबर्हिणवाजितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The glorious king of dharma, also enraged, pierced the king of Madras with sharp arrows fletched with heron and peacock feathers."}},{"n":52,"text":"चन्द्रसेनं च सप्तत्या सूतं च नवभिः शरैः ।\nद्रुमसेनं चतुःषष्ट्या निजघान महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great warrior pierced Chandrasena with seventy arrows and his charioteer with nine, and killed Drumasena with sixty-four."}},{"n":53,"text":"चक्ररक्षे हते शल्यः पाण्डवेन महात्मना ।\nनिजघान ततो राजंश्चेदीन्वै पञ्चविंशतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the wheel-guard was killed by the great-souled Pandava, Shalya then killed twenty-five Chedis, O king."}},{"n":54,"text":"सात्यकिं पञ्चविंशत्या भीमसेनं च पञ्चभिः ।\nमाद्रीपुत्रौ शतेनाजौ विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the fight he pierced Satyaki with twenty-five sharp arrows, Bhimasena with five, and the two sons of Madri with a hundred."}},{"n":55,"text":"एवं विचरतस्तस्य संग्रामे राजसत्तम ।\nसंप्रेषयच्छितान्पार्थः शरानाशीविषोपमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Shalya moved about so in the battle, best of kings, the son of Pritha sent sharp arrows like venomous snakes at him."}},{"n":56,"text":"ध्वजाग्रं चास्य समरे कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nप्रमुखे वर्तमानस्य भल्लेनापहरद्रथात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In front of him, in the battle, Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, cut the tip of Shalya's banner from his chariot with a broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":57,"text":"पाण्डुपुत्रेण वै तस्य केतुं छिन्नं महात्मना ।\nनिपतन्तमपश्याम गिरिशृङ्गमिवाहतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw that banner, cut down by the great-souled son of Pandu, fall like a mountain peak struck down."}},{"n":58,"text":"ध्वजं निपतितं दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवं च व्यवस्थितम् ।\nसंक्रुद्धो मद्रराजोऽभूच्छरवर्षं मुमोच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his banner fallen and the Pandava standing firm, the king of Madras grew furious and let loose a shower of arrows."}},{"n":59,"text":"शल्यः सायकवर्षेण पर्जन्य इव वृष्टिमान् ।\nअभ्यवर्षदमेयात्मा क्षत्रियं क्षत्रियर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, of immeasurable spirit and the best of kshatriyas, rained showers of shafts on that kshatriya, like Parjanya raining."}},{"n":60,"text":"सात्यकिं भीमसेनं च माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nएकैकं पञ्चभिर्विद्ध्वा युधिष्ठिरमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Satyaki, Bhimasena and the two Pandava sons of Madri with five arrows each, and then tormented Yudhishthira."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततो बाणमयं जालं विततं पाण्डवोरसि ।\nअपश्याम महाराज मेघजालमिवोद्गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then we saw a net of arrows spread over the Pandava's chest, great king, like a mass of clouds rising."}},{"n":62,"text":"तस्य शल्यो रणे क्रुद्धो बाणैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nदिशः प्रच्छादयामास प्रदिशश्च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious in the battle, the great warrior Shalya covered all directions and the in-between directions with arrows with bent joints."}},{"n":63,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा बाणजालेन पीडितः ।\nबभूव हृतविक्रान्तो जम्भो वृत्रहणा यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, pained by that net of arrows, lost his strength, like Jambha when slain by the slayer of Vritra."}}]}]}